defines a TLS extension\n   that allows endpoints to negotiate a larger maximum inner plaintext\n   size, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing overhead.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-05-07T16:46:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 406821, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/406821/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-11-03T16:46:34Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.\n   Records also have a 3-byte overhead due to the fixed opaque_type and\n   legacy_record_version fields.  This document defines a TLS extension\n   that allows endpoints to negotiate a larger maximum inner plaintext\n   size, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing overhead.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-05-07T16:46:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 407229, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/407229/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/41/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-11-04T14:55:41Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.\n   Records also have a 3-byte overhead due to the fixed opaque_type and\n   legacy_record_version fields.  This document defines a TLS extension\n   that allows endpoints to negotiate a larger maximum inner plaintext\n   size, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing overhead.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-05-07T16:46:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 409932, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/409932/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2025-12-04T14:05:56Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.\n   Records also have a 3-byte overhead due to the fixed opaque_type and\n   legacy_record_version fields.  This document defines a TLS extension\n   that allows endpoints to negotiate a larger maximum inner plaintext\n   size, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing overhead.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-05-07T16:46:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 409933, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/409933/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2025-12-04T14:06:12Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.\n   Records also have a 3-byte overhead due to the fixed opaque_type and\n   legacy_record_version fields.  This document defines a TLS extension\n   that allows endpoints to negotiate a larger maximum inner plaintext\n   size, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing overhead.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-05-07T16:46:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 419579, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/419579/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2026-04-06T15:47:36Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.\n   Records also have a 3-byte overhead due to the fixed opaque_type and\n   legacy_record_version fields.  This document defines a TLS extension\n   that allows endpoints to negotiate a larger maximum inner plaintext\n   size, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing overhead.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-05-07T16:46:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 419580, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/419580/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2026-04-06T15:49:18Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.  DTLS\n   1.3 uses the same plaintext size limit.  This document defines a TLS\n   extension that allows endpoints to advertise larger per-direction\n   maximum inner plaintext sizes, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing\n   overhead in TLS 1.3 and DTLS 1.3 record headers.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-10-09T07:57:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 419629, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/419629/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2026-04-07T07:57:07Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.  DTLS\n   1.3 uses the same plaintext size limit.  This document defines a TLS\n   extension that allows endpoints to advertise larger per-direction\n   maximum inner plaintext sizes, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing\n   overhead in TLS 1.3 and DTLS 1.3 record headers.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "expires": "2026-10-09T07:57:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 455536, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/455536/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2026-10-09T07:09:04Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}